1
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:12,150
A shop takes 0.1 of the price off in a sale.

2
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,260
A jacket costs 85 dollars.

3
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:17,640
A phone app works out 85 times 0.1.

4
00:00:17,690 --> 00:00:21,580
Will the answer be bigger or smaller than 85?

5
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:23,270
What is 85 times 0.1?

6
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:27,260
Pause the video and work it out.

7
00:00:27,310 --> 00:00:28,860
0.1 is one tenth.

8
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:32,460
So 85 times 0.1 means one tenth of 85.

9
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:36,690
That is 85 divided by 10, which is 8.5.

10
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:39,100
The discount is 8 dollars 50.

11
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:43,220
Multiplying by 0.1 made the answer smaller.

12
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:48,680
Remember: when you multiply by 10, the digits move one place to the left.

13
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:53,560
When you divide by 100, they move two places to the right.

14
00:00:53,610 --> 00:00:57,980
So 3.6 divided by 100 is 0.036.

15
00:00:58,030 --> 00:00:59,410
0.1 is one tenth.

16
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:04,330
So multiplying by 0.1 is the same as dividing by 10.

17
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:06,330
0.01 is one hundredth.

18
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:11,780
So multiplying by 0.01 is the same as dividing by 100.

19
00:01:11,830 --> 00:01:15,460
For example, 46 times 0.1 is 4.6.

20
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:18,910
And 46 times 0.01 is 0.46.

21
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:19,720
Your turn.

22
00:01:19,770 --> 00:01:21,500
Work out 7 times 0.01.

23
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:25,090
Pause the video and try it.

24
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:29,290
Times 0.01 is the same as divide by 100.

25
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:32,460
7 divided by 100 is 0.07.

26
00:01:32,510 --> 00:01:33,510
Now dividing.

27
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:36,010
How many tenths are there in 3?

28
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:38,760
There are 10 in each whole, so 30.

29
00:01:38,810 --> 00:01:43,510
So dividing by 0.1 is the same as multiplying by 10.

30
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:46,620
How many hundredths are there in 3?

31
00:01:46,670 --> 00:01:46,970
300.

32
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:52,320
So dividing by 0.01 is the same as multiplying by 100.

33
00:01:52,370 --> 00:01:57,310
Dividing by a number between 0 and 1 makes the answer bigger.

34
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:59,070
Here is the method.

35
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:02,500
Step 1: times 0.1 means divide by 10.

36
00:02:02,550 --> 00:02:05,930
Times 0.01 means divide by 100.

37
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:09,590
Step 2: divide by 0.1 means times 10.

38
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:13,220
Divide by 0.01 means times 100.

39
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:16,490
Step 3: move the digits the right way.

40
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:17,490
Step 4: check.

41
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:21,690
Multiplying by a number less than 1 gives a smaller answer.

42
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:24,870
Dividing by it gives a bigger answer.

43
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:27,950
Work out 0.45 divided by 0.1.

44
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,710
Divide by 0.1 is times 10.

45
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,490
0.45 times 10 is 4.5.

46
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:34,280
Your turn.

47
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:36,510
Work out 2.3 divided by 0.1.

48
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:39,660
Pause and work it out.

49
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:42,300
Divide by 0.1 is times 10.

50
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:44,240
2.3 times 10 is 23.

51
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:47,540
There are 23 tenths in 2.3.

52
00:02:47,590 --> 00:02:51,660
Work out 7.2 times 0.01, divided by 0.1.

53
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:56,960
Times 0.01 is divide by 100: that gives 0.072.

54
00:02:57,010 --> 00:03:01,040
Then divide by 0.1, which is times 10.

55
00:03:01,090 --> 00:03:04,060
0.072 times 10 is 0.72.

56
00:03:04,110 --> 00:03:06,050
Find the missing number.

57
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:07,870
53 times what is 0.53?

58
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:11,280
The digits moved two places to the right.

59
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:16,400
That is divide by 100, which is the same as times 0.01.

60
00:03:16,450 --> 00:03:18,810
Raj works out 6 divided by 0.1.

61
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:21,540
Which line goes wrong first?

62
00:03:21,590 --> 00:03:22,860
Line 1 is wrong.

63
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:28,160
There are 10 tenths in every whole, so there are 60 tenths in 6.

64
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:31,860
Divide by 0.1 is the same as times 10.

65
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:34,930
6 divided by 0.1 is 60.

66
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:37,160
1 cent is 0.01 of a dollar.

67
00:03:37,210 --> 00:03:41,840
So to change cents into dollars, multiply by 0.01.

68
00:03:41,890 --> 00:03:44,620
A jar holds 4,750 cents.

69
00:03:44,670 --> 00:03:47,520
4,750 times 0.01 is 47.5.

70
00:03:47,570 --> 00:03:50,620
That is 47 dollars 50.

71
00:03:50,670 --> 00:03:52,120
One last question.

72
00:03:52,170 --> 00:03:59,220
Which gives the biggest answer: 5 divided by 0.01, 5 times 0.01, or 5 divided by 0.1?

73
00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:02,870
Pause the video and choose.

74
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:05,630
5 divided by 0.01 is 500.

75
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,950
5 times 0.01 is 0.05.

76
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,490
5 divided by 0.1 is 50.

77
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:14,680
The biggest is 5 divided by 0.01.

78
00:04:14,730 --> 00:04:19,150
To remember: times 0.1 is the same as divide by 10.

79
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:23,200
Times 0.01 is the same as divide by 100.

80
00:04:23,250 --> 00:04:26,600
Divide by 0.1 is the same as times 10.

81
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:30,730
Divide by 0.01 is the same as times 100.

82
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:35,700
Multiplying by a number less than 1 makes the answer smaller.

83
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:40,300
Dividing by a number less than 1 makes the answer bigger.

84
00:04:40,350 --> 00:04:45,470
Great work! Now practise lesson 3.1 on Camday.
